MerkleCapitalFlowTest
├── given the production vault and delegator
│   ├── when allocated cash is invested
│   │   └── it is usable immediately but requires a covering report before return
│   ├── when a report arrives after an already released withdrawal
│   │   └── it excludes the completed return exactly once
│   ├── when allocations coincide with outstanding demand
│   │   └── it retains all allocated capital without an unreported refund
│   ├── when lifetime realized returns exceed allocations
│   │   └── it preserves negative signed net capital after reported release
│   ├── when a full exit realizes a loss
│   │   └── it recognizes the loss before releasing cash
│   ├── when half the vault shares request exit before a twenty percent loss
│   │   └── the real queue pays 4000 and leaves 4000 to the other half
│   ├── when returned cash arrives after a delayed snapshot
│   │   └── it remains locked until a later covering report
│   ├── when repeated staging calls and partial returns span snapshots
│   │   └── it preserves the fixed first stage and releases later cash in later batches
│   ├── when a curator exits through the public delegator and account management
│   │   ├── it caps the request at NAV and lowers the absolute allocation limit to zero
│   │   ├── it keeps managed returns locked until a covering report is accepted
│   │   └── it conserves vault assets and revokes adapter roles on removal
│   ├── when a curator exit overlaps withdrawal queue demand
│   │   ├── it replaces the force request with cumulative queue demand during the public sweep
│   │   ├── it fills and pays the queue after a covering report while preserving the remaining NAV
│   │   └── it completes the remaining public exit and removes the adapter after another covering report
│   └── when the accepted NAV expires
│       └── it rolls back the token transfer and flow checkpoint
└── given stateful public delegator operations
    ├── when public allocation or deallocation sweeps released cash
    │   └── it includes every completed transfer in the independent ghost model
    ├── when losses occur before and after a delayed snapshot
    │   └── it recognizes only snapshot-covered losses while tracking later losses independently
    ├── when withdrawal demand is cancelled or capital moves before delivery
    │   └── it preserves staging coverage and reconciles every completed vault transfer
    ├── when a cached snapshot expires or NAV becomes stale
    │   └── it refreshes the captured losses and discards the old pending report
    ├── when report capture advances time near NAV expiry
    │   └── it keeps NAV fresh and preserves the pending report
    ├── when the account loses all its cash and later earns profit
    │   └── it writes down NAV to zero and accounts for the new profit
    ├── it keeps flow-adjusted NAV equal to portfolio custody plus unreported losses
    ├── it keeps staged and released liquidity backed by adapter cash and the staged block in sync
    └── it conserves combined custody after profits and losses while NAV retains unreported losses
